{{project}}
============

API server generated by TurboGears2 quickstart-api command.

This project demonstrates best practices for implementing JSON-based APIs with TurboGears2.

Features
--------

- **RESTful API**: Clean REST controller implementation with ``tg.RestController``
- **Dual Authentication**: Support for both cookie-based and Bearer token authentication
- **Automatic OpenAPI**: API documentation automatically generated via ``tgext.apispec``
- **Validation**: Automatic parameter validation with ``@validate`` decorator
- **JSON Responses**: Native JSON support with proper content-type headers

Quick Start
----------

1. Install the project in development mode::

    pip install -e '.[testing]'

2. Run the test suite::

    python -m pytest

3. Initialize the database and create demo users::

    gearbox setup-app

3. Run the development server::

    gearbox serve --reload --debug

4. Open your browser to http://localhost:8080 to see the API demo page.

API Endpoints
-------------

- ``GET /api/movies`` - List all movies
- ``POST /api/movies`` - Create a new movie
- ``GET /api/movies/{id}`` - Get a specific movie
- ``PUT /api/movies/{id}`` - Update a movie
- ``DELETE /api/movies/{id}`` - Delete a movie (via POST /api/movies/{id}/_delete)
- ``GET /demo/admin`` - Admin-only endpoint (requires 'manage' permission)
- ``GET /api/openapi.json`` - OpenAPI specification
- ``GET /api/docs`` - Interactive API documentation (Redoc)

Authentication
--------------

This API supports two authentication methods:

1. **Bearer Token**: Use the ``Authorization: Bearer <token>`` header
2. **Cookie Auth**: Use the standard TurboGears login flow

Demo users created by ``gearbox setup-app``:

- **manager**: password=managepass, token=abc123def456ghi789jkl012mno345 (has 'manage' permission)
- **editor**: password=editpass, token=pqr678stu901vwx234yz567abc890

Example using Bearer token::

    curl -H "Authorization: Bearer abc123def456ghi789jkl012mno345" http://localhost:8080/api/movies

Example using cookie auth::

    # Login first
    curl -v --cookie-jar cookies.txt -d "login=manager&password=managepass" http://localhost:8080/login_handler
    
    # Then access API with cookie
    curl --cookie cookies.txt http://localhost:8080/demo/admin

Cleanup
-------

Once you're ready to build your own API, you can remove the demo parts::

    rm -rf controllers/api/movies.py controllers/demo.py model/movie.py

And remove the demo imports from ``controllers/root.py`` and ``model/__init__.py``.

